      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781083423556,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "JSX is syntax extension for javascript, although I have seen in multiple websites they are \nusing Javascript XML, but I haven't seen anything like this in react documentation.\nit can be JSX  Javascript extension. because multiple times in programing we use x in sort for\nthe word starting with ex like executable and all.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "JSX is syntax extension for javascript, although I have seen in multiple websites they are \nusing Javascript XML, but I haven't seen anything like this in react documentation.\nit can be JSX  Javascript extension. because multiple times in programing we use x in sort for\nthe word starting with ex like executable and all.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
