    {
      "id": "F54weMi-SLZJNVEsA-3gO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1151.2729157911454,
      "y": 94820.78700969061,
      "width": 1056,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bs5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1692207850,
      "version": 362,
      "versionNonce": 37536787,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781083423556,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "const App = () => {\n\nconst Child = () => {\n            return <h1>child</h1>\n    }\n\n\n} \n\nreturn (\n    <div>\n        <h1> Parent </h1>\n        <Child/>\n\n    </div>\n)\n\n\n\nthis will work, but in good practice we should not do this because it can slow our application. \nwe can create another component in  same file and use that inside other.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "const App = () => {\n\nconst Child = () => {\n            return <h1>child</h1>\n    }\n\n\n} \n\nreturn (\n    <div>\n        <h1> Parent </h1>\n        <Child/>\n\n    </div>\n)\n\n\n\nthis will work, but in good practice we should not do this because it can slow our application. \nwe can create another component in  same file and use that inside other.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
